      <description>The political drama resulting from Democrats’ landslide midterm victory will start in early December with budget talks, especially those focused on defense spending. The plot is as tangled as a daytime soap opera. Legislators have already taken a stab at removing Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth, and the Iran war hangs over negotiations like a dark, ominous cloud.</description>
